 a strong democratic  incumbent  and  what happens when you have districts  like that where an incumbent does not  run whether it's a republican or  democrat by the way  you have to spend more money  on an unknown than you would on an  incumbent so that race even if you win  it is going to take more resources to be  able to win it  so that's a big drain on the democrats  so how do they fix this  obviously the easy answer you deliver  for the american public  they got the child tax credit going out  right now that's great  you're showing people look we are giving  you money  we're giving you money to help you  through this pandemic  so that's a positive the reconciliation  bill three and a half trillion dollars  depending on whether or not cinema and  mansion shave off some of that that  includes real tangible benefits for  pretty much every single district here  in the united states that is a must-pass  piece of legislation  and honestly i think the midterms are  going to hinge on what happens with that  reconciliation bill  if you make promises to the public as  joe biden did they promise get rid of  some student loan debt they've done a  little  but not in any kind of widespread way  that affects a lot of people  and that's unfortunate that could come  back to bite you  so if you deliver big time with this  reconciliation bill and you give people  something tangible something they can  either hold or see for themselves that  you have done  you just might stave off what could be a  midterm bloodbath  for the democratic party  so  that's where it is you know what to do  so get busy on it  i'm faring cousins in for david pakman  we'll be right back
 

